namespace Magma

/-- A member of the class, as the `3` orbit values it takes together with the proof that they name
one. `Magma.tupOK` is three tests: every orbit value is one the group's action allows, the operation
the tuple builds really is invariant, and no excess permutation is an automorphism of it. -/
@[reducible] def tup11R314 : Type := {w : Fin 3 → Fin 11 // Magma.tupOK S11R314.E S11R314.tr S11R314.z S11R314.st S11R314.X w = true}

/-- The class, as a family of magmas indexed by its own membership test. -/
@[implicit_reducible]
def srch11R314 (v : tup11R314) : Magma (Fin 11) :=
  Magma.mk (Magma.transport S11R314.E S11R314.tr v.1)

end Magma

/-! ### The source exhibits

`4` members of the class, chosen by greedy cover so that between them they model all `4` equations
that have a model in the class at all. Each check is `Magma.tupOK`: the tuple names a member of the
class. It is `decide!` rather than `decide` because the invariance test is `121` cells times the
`55` group elements, which the elaborator will not walk inside its heartbeat limit.
-/

