/-! ### The exhibits, spelled out

`Magma.transport` reads a cell as `E (tr x y).2 (v (tr x y).1)`, so the kernel walks the `55`-row
group table once per cell -- and a `Satisfies` certificate on `Fin 11` asks for `14,641` cells.
Below is the same operation as a plain `11 x 11` table, checked once against `Magma.transport` by
`native_decide`, so that the certificates in `Definability/Certs/Srch11R314Sources*.lean` can be
`decide!` against the table instead. Without this the two heaviest classes were killed at `55 GB`.
-/

